  "instructions": "Produce an analysis plan for this task by selecting components from the catalogue and setting their parameters. Use only catalogue component ids and declared parameter options; omitted parameters take their defaults. Deterministic code executes the plan exactly as written, and the result is scored against a frozen rubric (correctness, completeness, reproducibility, statistical discipline, communication) and a frozen golden reference. List in skills_applied the ids of any provided skills you actually used.",
  "payload": {
    "task_id": "T6",
    "condition": "baseline",
    "task_spec": {
      "task_id": "T6",
      "title": "Baseline fraud model",
      "objective": "Train a baseline classifier for the synthetic fraud label on the medical claims: logistic regression plus one tree-based model. Hold out a quarter of the claims with a split that preserves the class balance in both partitions, using the run seed, and report the positive-class prevalence in each partition. Use only features that would be legitimately available at prediction time: exclude identifiers and any field that is derived from the label. Fit every preprocessing step (encoding, scaling) on the training partition only. Report precision, recall, F1, PR-AUC, ROC-AUC and the confusion matrix for each model on the held-out partition, save the final feature list, and state the limitations: synthetic label, class imbalance, a baseline model, and no operational use.",
      "tags": [
        "modeling",
        "fraud",
        "classification",
        "leakage",
        "splits",
        "seeds",
        "metrics",
        "class_imbalance"
      ],
      "input_tables": [
        "medical_claims"
      ],
      "required_artifacts": [
        "model_metrics.json",
        "confusion_matrices.png",
        "pr_curves.png",
        "feature_list.json",
        "report.md",
        "metrics.json"
      ]
    },
    "component_catalogue": [
